**Release audit checkpoint — 2026-11-07, origin/main `94e1c11f7`** (0.3 row: "Required core/Runtime/Module/Adapter/compiler prerequisites" → independent definitions, ledger maps this issue).

Scope child — **落实 Compiler 与原型独立定义约束** — is not met at main. Live evidence of boundary violations:
- `packages/compiler/src/react.ts:142-144` emits consumer imports of `@proto.ui/prototypes-base/transition` (compiler output binds to prototype package surfaces);
- `packages/compiler/src/conformance/button-cases.ts:671` hardcodes prototype source path `packages/prototypes/base/src/button/button.proto.ts` as conformance `source`;
- `packages/compiler/test/fixtures/button-ssr/button.proto.ts:2` imports `../../../../prototypes/base/src/button/button.proto` (`asButton`) — a test-fixture dependency, acceptable as test-only, but it documents the shared-definition pattern the constraint forbids in compiler runtime paths;
- prototypes depend only on `@proto.ui/{core,hooks,types,module-*}` (verified `packages/prototypes/base/package.json`) — the prototype→compiler direction is clean.

Box checked: **0/1** — constraint not enforced on the compiler side.

Next executable action: **proto-compiler pane slice** — remove the compiler-runtime prototype-surface bindings (`react.ts` transition import emission + `button-cases.ts` hardcoded source), replacing with compiler-owned IR/config inputs; per issue body, compiler/IR delivery routes through the proto-compiler pane. Prior 0.4-deferral superseded by `release-0.3-list.md` committed scope (prerequisite row names #1145).
